{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://shorts-maker/schemas/visual_features_v1.schema.json",
  "title": "visual_features_v1",
  "description": "Phase 4 visual analysis (owner decision 2026-10-07 s4-s6). face: MediaPipe Face Detection model_selection=1, min_detection_confidence=0.5 at FACE_SAMPLE_FPS=5 (face_runtime@1 -- currently BLOCKED_BY_DEPENDENCY); motion: Farneback on grayscale frames, dimensionless motion = mean(flow magnitude)/frame_diagonal at 2 fps; screen: deterministic Canny/contour detector at 1 fps. No audio-only or no-video source applies (a source always has video; validate_source). Body carries identity/provenance that is not circular; artifact_id, checksum, created_at and storage_location live on the Artifact row (impl plan 3.1) exactly as for transcript_v1 -- a checksum inside the bytes it hashes is impossible and created_at would break content addressing. (Flagged for owner confirmation, Phase-4 review.) OPEN (asked of owner): whether the 10 fps motion_event_probe series must be persisted here for Phase 9 hook.first_motion_ms, and which robust-z baseline motion_z uses (60 s rolling for peaks vs video-level for vis.motion_mean_z / hook).",
